                                        <td style="text-align:center;color:#16a34a;font-weight:700;">✓ From any device</td>
                                        <td style="text-align:center;color:#d97706;">Limited (TeamViewer etc.)</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><strong>Multiple MT4 instances</strong></td>
                                        <td style="text-align:center;color:#16a34a;font-weight:700;">✓ Easy to scale</td>
                                        <td style="text-align:center;color:#d97706;">Limited by RAM/CPU</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><strong>Hardware maintenance</strong></td>
                                        <td style="text-align:center;color:#16a34a;font-weight:700;">✓ Provider managed</td>
                                        <td style="text-align:center;color:#ef4444;">Your responsibility</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><strong>Monthly cost</strong></td>
                                        <td style="text-align:center;color:#d97706;">$10–$50/month</td>
                                        <td style="text-align:center;color:#16a34a;font-weight:700;">$0 (already have PC)</td>
                                    </tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>

                        <div class="br-divider"></div>

                        @* Section 4 — Who Needs It *@
                        <div class="br-section" id="s4">
                            <h2 class="br-h2">4. Who Actually Needs a Forex VPS?</h2>
                            <p class="br-p">A VPS is not necessary for every trader. Here is an honest breakdown of which trading profiles genuinely benefit vs those who can comfortably trade without one.</p>

                            <div class="br-pros-cons">
                                <div class="br-pros">
                                    <div class="br-pros-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-server me-2"></i>VPS Is Essential If You…</div>
                                    <ul style="margin:0;padding:0 0 0 18px;line-height:2.4;font-size:14px;color:#374151;">
                                        <li>Run Expert Advisors (EAs) or automated bots</li>
                                        <li>Use scalping strategies with tight entry timing</li>
                                        <li>Need to manage open trades while away from your desk</li>
                                        <li>Have unreliable home internet or power supply</li>
                                        <li>Trade across multiple accounts simultaneously</li>
                                        <li>Run copy trading software or signal services</li>
                                        <li>Use trailing stop EAs that must react in real time</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                                <div class="br-cons">
                                    <div class="br-cons-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-user me-2"></i>VPS May Not Be Needed If You…</div>
                                    <ul style="margin:0;padding:0 0 0 18px;line-height:2.4;font-size:14px;color:#374151;">
                                        <li>Trade manually only during London/NY market hours</li>
                                        <li>Place swing trades with wide stops that don't need precision</li>
                                        <li>Always monitor your trades in real time at your desk</li>
                                        <li>Use a broker's guaranteed stop-loss feature</li>
                                        <li>Have stable, fast home internet (&lt;50ms to broker)</li>
                                        <li>Trade infrequently (1–5 trades per week)</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="br-divider"></div>

                        @* Section 5 — Latency *@
                        <div class="br-section" id="s5">
                            <h2 class="br-h2">5. How VPS Reduces Execution Latency</h2>
                            <p class="br-p">Latency is the time between your EA sending an order and the broker's server receiving and filling it. Every millisecond of delay can result in slippage — being filled at a worse price than your EA intended. For scalpers and HFT strategies, this difference is the margin between profit and loss.</p>

                            <div class="br-highlights" style="border-color:#a5f3fc;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfeff,#cffafe);">
                                <div class="br-highlights-title" style="color:#0e7490;"><i class="fa-solid fa-bolt me-2"></i>Latency Comparison</div>
                                <ul style="margin:0;padding:0 0 0 18px;line-height:2.2;font-size:14px;color:#374151;">
                                    <li><strong>Home broadband (UK/EU):</strong> 50–100ms to London broker servers</li>
                                    <li><strong>Home broadband (Asia/AUS):</strong> 100–250ms to London/New York servers</li>
                                    <li><strong>VPS in London (same DC as broker):</strong> 1–5ms — negligible latency</li>
                                    <li><strong>VPS in New York (NY4/NY5 data centres):</strong> 1–3ms to US brokers</li>
                                    <li><strong>Slippage impact at 100ms latency:</strong> 0.5–2 pips on fast markets</li>
                                    <li><strong>Slippage impact at 5ms latency:</strong> Near-zero on most order types</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>

                            <p class="br-p">For swing traders placing 1–5 trades per week on H4 charts, a 100ms delay is meaningless. For a scalping EA firing 50 trades per day on M1 charts, a 100ms vs 5ms difference in execution can represent hundreds of dollars in recovered slippage per month.</p>

                            <div class="br-callout">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb me-2" style="color:#d97706;"></i>
                                <strong>Pro tip:</strong> Ask your broker which data centre their servers are in (Equinix NY4, LD4, TY3 are common). Choose a VPS provider with a node in the same or adjacent facility for lowest possible latency.
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="br-divider"></div>

                        @* Section 6 — Setup Steps *@
                        <div class="br-section" id="s6">
                            <h2 class="br-h2">6. How to Set Up MT4/MT5 on a VPS — Step by Step</h2>
                            <p class="br-p">Setting up a trading VPS takes around 20–30 minutes. Here is the complete process from signing up to running your first EA.</p>

                            <div class="ptb-step-flow">
                                @foreach (var s in setupSteps)
                                {
                                    <div class="ptb-step">
                                        <div class="ptb-step-num" style="background:@s.Bg;color:@s.Color;">@s.Num</div>
                                        <div class="ptb-step-body">
                                            <div class="ptb-step-icon" style="background:@s.Bg;color:@s.Color;"><i class="@s.Icon"></i></div>
                                            <div class="ptb-step-content">
                                                <div class="ptb-step-title">@s.Title</div>
                                                <div class="ptb-step-text">@s.Body</div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                }
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="br-divider"></div>

                        @* Section 7 — VPS Plans *@
                        <div class="br-section" id="s7">
                            <h2 class="br-h2">7. Choosing the Right VPS Plan for Your Trading</h2>
                            <p class="br-p">The right VPS specification depends entirely on how many MT4/MT5 instances and EAs you need to run simultaneously. Each MT4 terminal with a few active EAs typically uses 200–400 MB of RAM.</p>

                            <div class="row g-3">
                                @foreach (var v in vpsSpecs)
                                {
                                    <div class="col-md-6">
                                        <div class="ptb-account-card" style="border-color:@v.Border;background:@v.Bg;">
                                            <div class="ptb-account-hd" style="color:@v.Color;">
                                                <i class="fa-solid fa-server ptb-account-icon"></i>
                                                <div>
                                                    <div class="ptb-account-type">@v.Plan</div>
                                                    <div class="ptb-account-balance">@v.Price</div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                            <div class="ptb-account-tag" style="background:@v.Color;color:#fff;">@v.BestFor</div>
                                            <div class="ptb-account-rows">
                                                <div class="ptb-account-row"><span>RAM</span><span class="ptb-account-row-val" style="color:@v.Color;">@v.RAM</span></div>
                                                <div class="ptb-account-row"><span>CPU</span><span class="ptb-account-row-val" style="color:@v.Color;">@v.CPU</span></div>
                                                <div class="ptb-account-row"><span>Storage</span><span class="ptb-account-row-val" style="color:@v.Color;">@v.Storage</span></div>
                                                <div class="ptb-account-row"><span>EA Capacity</span><span class="ptb-account-row-val" style="color:@v.Color;">@v.EAs</span></div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                }
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="br-divider"></div>

                        @* Section 8 — Free VPS *@
                        <div class="br-section" id="s8">
                            <h2 class="br-h2">8. Can You Get a Free VPS from Your Broker?</h2>
                            <p class="br-p">Yes — many cashback-eligible brokers offer free VPS access to clients who meet a minimum monthly trading volume. This is one of the best-kept cost-saving secrets in retail forex trading.</p>

                            <div class="br-platform-grid" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;">
                                <div class="br-platform-card">
                                    <div class="br-platform-icon" style="color:#0891b2;background:#ecfeff;"><i class="fa-solid fa-gift"></i></div>
                                    <div>
                                        <div class="br-platform-name">IC Markets — Free VPS</div>
                                        <div class="br-platform-desc">IC Markets offers a free VPS to clients who maintain an account balance of $2,000+ or trade a minimum of 5 standard lots per month. The VPS is hosted at Equinix NY4 and LD4 data centres — the same facilities as their servers — ensuring ultra-low latency execution for EA traders.</div>
                                        <div class="br-platform-tags">
                                            <span class="br-platform-tag">Min 5 lots/month</span>
                                            <span class="br-platform-tag">Equinix LD4 / NY4</span>
                                            <span class="br-platform-tag">Windows Server</span>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="br-platform-card">
                                    <div class="br-platform-icon" style="color:#16a34a;background:#f0fdf4;"><i class="fa-solid fa-server"></i></div>
                                    <div>
                                        <div class="br-platform-name">PU Prime — VPS Access</div>
                                        <div class="br-platform-desc">PU Prime provides VPS hosting solutions for active traders. Contact your account manager or check the client portal for current VPS eligibility criteria based on your account tier and monthly trading volume.</div>
                                        <div class="br-platform-tags">
                                            <span class="br-platform-tag">Volume-based</span>
                                            <span class="br-platform-tag">MT4 &amp; MT5</span>
                                            <span class="br-platform-tag">Ask Account Manager</span>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="br-platform-card">
                                    <div class="br-platform-icon" style="color:#7c3aed;background:#f5f3ff;"><i class="fa-solid fa-building-columns"></i></div>
                                    <div>
                                        <div class="br-platform-name">Third-Party VPS Providers</div>
                                        <div class="br-platform-desc">If your broker doesn't offer a free VPS, use a specialist forex VPS provider such as ForexVPS.net, BeeksFX, or FXVM. These providers are optimised specifically for MetaTrader with Windows Server environments, low-latency network connections to major broker data centres, and 24/7 monitoring.</div>
                                        <div class="br-platform-tags">
