                        @* Section 10 — Mistakes *@
                        <div class="br-section" id="s10">
                            <h2 class="br-h2">10. Common VPS Mistakes to Avoid</h2>
                            <p class="br-p">Many traders get a VPS but then undermine its benefits with simple setup and management errors. Avoid these common pitfalls.</p>

                            <div class="psc-mistake-grid">
                                <div class="psc-mistake-card">
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark"></i></div>
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-title">Choosing the Wrong Server Location</div>
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-body">A VPS in Australia connecting to a London broker defeats the purpose — latency will be worse than a good home connection. Always choose a VPS in the same city or data centre as your broker.</div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="psc-mistake-card">
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark"></i></div>
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-title">Under-Specifying RAM for Multiple EAs</div>
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-body">Running 5 MT4 instances on a 1 GB RAM VPS will cause crashes and slowdowns. Allow 300–500 MB per MT4 instance plus 512 MB for Windows Server overhead.</div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="psc-mistake-card">
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark"></i></div>
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-title">Not Enabling MT4 Auto-Restart</div>
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-body">Configure MT4/MT5 to start automatically on Windows boot (Task Scheduler or Startup folder). If the VPS restarts for updates, your EA must resume trading without manual intervention.</div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="psc-mistake-card">
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark"></i></div>
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-title">Forgetting to Check EA Status</div>
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-body">EAs can stop running silently — due to broker disconnection, MT4 update prompts, or errors. Schedule a weekly RDP check-in to verify all EAs are active and trading as expected.</div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="psc-mistake-card">
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark"></i></div>
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-title">Using a General-Purpose VPS</div>
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-body">Generic cloud VPS (AWS, DigitalOcean) can work but are not optimised for trading. Forex-specific VPS providers offer pre-configured Windows Server environments with MT4 pre-installed and trading-optimised network routes.</div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="psc-mistake-card">
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark"></i></div>
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-title">Skipping Position Sizing on the VPS EA</div>
                                    <div class="psc-mistake-body">EAs running on a VPS trade real money 24/7. Never deploy an EA without confirming its lot size and risk settings. A misconfigured EA can lose your account in hours while you're unaware.</div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

